---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { EXERCISES } from '../../server/exercises/index.js';
import { MODULES, TRACKS, ALL_LESSONS } from '../../content/curriculum.js';

// Still a placeholder for the real positioning work in section 5 of ROADMAP.md
// - what it now has is a way through to the course, which it did not before.
const count = EXERCISES.length;
---
<Doc
  wide
  title="MongoDB Practice — learn and run MongoDB queries in your browser"
  description="A MongoDB course with 54 lessons and 38 auto-graded exercises that tell you exactly which field of your result is wrong. No signup, no install, no database."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Learn MongoDB by running queries, not reading about them</h1>
    <p>
      {ALL_LESSONS.length} lessons across {MODULES.length} modules, and {count} hand-written
      exercises graded against a live reference solution. Get one wrong and it tells you
      <em>which field</em> was wrong — not just that you were.
    </p>
    <p class="sub">No signup. No install. No database. Queries run in this tab.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/learn/">Start the course →</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/practice/">Jump straight to the exercises</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>The course</h2>
    <span class="meta">{ALL_LESSONS.length} lessons · {count} drills</span>
  </div>
  <div class="grid">
    {TRACKS.map((t) => (
      <a class="card" href="/learn/">
        <div class="card-row">
          <h3>{t.title}</h3>
          <span class="meta">{MODULES.filter((m) => m.track === t.slug).length} modules</span>
        </div>
        <p>{t.summary}</p>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>Why this one</h2></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>It says what was wrong</h3>
      <p>
        Not "incorrect". <code>row 0.revenue: expected 53000, got 27000</code> — the
        field, the expected value and yours.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Graded against a live solution</h3>
      <p>
        Answers are not stored JSON that goes stale. The reference query runs against
        the same data as yours, every time.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Nothing leaves your browser</h3>
      <p>
        The <a href="/dataset/">dataset</a> is built in your tab from a fixed seed. There
        is no server to send a query to.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Hand-written, not generated</h3>
      <p>
        {count} exercises, each a distinct concept. No padding the count with the same
        question and a different product name.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="soon-note">
    Coming soon, through a local <code>npx</code> mode: connect your own MongoDB,
    <code>explain()</code>, and index tuning.
  </p>
</Doc>

<style>
  .hero { margin: 4vh 0 10px; max-width: 40rem; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 5vw, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .hero p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-soft); }
  .hero .sub { font-size: .9rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .hero em { color: var(--text); font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .grid .card { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .card-row .meta { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10.5px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .card code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    background: var(--panel-2);
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .card a { color: var(--accent); }

  .soon-note {
    margin: 34px 0 0;
    padding: 11px 14px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--line);
    border-radius: 7px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 12.5px;
  }
  .soon-note code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    background: var(--panel-2);
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
</style>
